{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Digestive system: basic parts and their jobs","theme":{"background":"#f5f9f2","foreground":"#1d3b2a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Mouth"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The mouth takes in food. Teeth chew it and saliva starts to break it down."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which part of the digestive system chews food into smaller pieces?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"The teeth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"The liver","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"The large intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which organ is a muscular tube that moves food down to the stomach?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The oesophagus","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The gall bladder","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The pancreas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Stomach"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-e","content":"The stomach churns food and mixes it with acid to break it down further."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"You eat a big lunch quickly. Which path do you choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Eat slowly and chew well","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Gulp it down without chewing","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Chewing mixes food with saliva, so your stomach has an easier job. Well done."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Big pieces are hard for the stomach to break down, so you may feel uncomfortable."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which organ absorbs most of the digested food into the blood?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"The small intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"The stomach","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"The mouth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which organ removes water from the waste before it leaves the body?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The large intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The small intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The oesophagus","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which organ makes bile, which helps digest fats?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"The liver","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"The stomach","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"The rectum","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the digestive system lesson"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Great work. You now know the main parts of the digestive system and what each one does."}],"actions":[]}}
